    verification delegatedCeremonyIsASkillReviewGate : Test { :>> id = "dcdadba8-27ec-4f8c-867b-e01f72a74825"; :>> title = "Sprint 699 review gate — three passes per D0172"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-13"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "Three passes (D0172). Correctness: the check mirrors the marker-vocabulary guard's declaration read (line-anchored metadata def, // lines skipped) so a marker it calls undeclared is one the guard would fail; the gate-line rule matches the two last-line shapes main.rs prints (gate: fast gate clean ... and gate: FAST GATE FAILED ...) plus the receipt-answered form; subagent_block_control is pure and relabels only a block. Honesty: the hook cannot see a recorder that leaves the tree red WITHOUT changing the fingerprint (nothing to gate) and cannot see one dispatched as general-purpose - the role is carried by the agent type, stated in the skill; the recorder still runs its own check, which is the residual the retro names. Scope: no schema, no guard, no ledger field (the ledger's frozen field set is untouched - the role rides in the control string); the test-verify skill is not modified."; }
