    verification delegatedCeremonyIsASkillRetroGate : Test { :>> id = "de74bdd2-d702-4f71-88b3-76b528959ac4"; :>> title = "Sprint 699 retro gate (autonomous, D0049)"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-13"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::analyze; :>> procedureText = "Two findings, each a tracked item. First: the recorder runs the report check on itself, and the SubagentStop payload carries last_assistant_message - the hook could run the same check over the recorder's actual last message and refuse a report that outran the gate, moving clause (c) from the recorder's discipline to a control; issue521 tracks it, resolved by dcSubagentStopChecksTheRecorderReport. Second: .claude/skills/brand-watch/check_manifest.py is a tracked file under the generated surface with no .engine/skills/brand-watch source, and sync-claude --check does not name it - an unsourced file under a generated surface is drift the guard should see; issue522 tracks it, resolved by dcClaudeSurfaceNamesUnsourcedFiles. D0131 avoidable-issue scan: the check's first run found #Addresses declared because a prose quotation of the guard's repair hint contained metadata def Addresses; - caught by running the pair before the tree was trusted (D0388 as designed), no new item. Third, observed on this sprint's own first dispatch: Claude Code loads .claude/agents/ at session start, so the verifier and recorder written this session could not be dispatched by type (Agent type 'verifier' not found) so the verifier ran as general-purpose under the same brief; the types appeared in the Agent tool some minutes later in the same session and the recorder was dispatched by type - a harness property, no new item. Fourth, from the verifier's own receipt: it named guard FAIL (154 violations) and sync-claude DRIFT that no current binary reproduces, because it ran target/release/keel-gate.exe - a six-day-stale copy at build e0624f3+dirty - instead of the binary the brief named; the receipt carries head= but no build=, so the substitution was invisible until the agent was asked; issue523 tracks it, resolved by dcStaleBinaryNamesItself, and the ten stale copies were deleted."; }
